{
  "rationale": "The plant automaton G1 models the robot's combined perception and motion capabilities, including all possible sensor outcomes and motion commands. The specification automata E1-E4 encode safe, coverage-biased exploration: E1 binds clear to forward/random_walk, E2 binds obstacle_front to a brief backward recovery, E3 binds obstacle_left/right to a directed turn, and E4 prevents repeated backward or full_rotate actions. The design ensures that the robot spends most time making forward progress, uses random_walk to avoid getting stuck, and only uses backward or full_rotate as last-resort recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model all perception and motion as a single plant automaton for determinism and compactness.",
    "Use separate specifications to enforce safe, coverage-oriented recovery and exploration, with minimal use of backward/full_rotate and strong bias toward forward/random_walk."
  ],
